      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Doerun was incorporated as a town by the Georgia General Assembly on December 22, 1899, enabling local governance.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/doerun_georgia",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The arrival of the Georgia Northern Railroad in 1898 turned Doerun from a modest settlement into a bustling cotton hub with gins and warehouses.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/doerun_georgia",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "By the 1920s, Doerun farmers began adding peanuts to cotton to guard against boll weevil damage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
